  "uprn": "100023490155",
  "decision_date": "23/12/2005",
  "description": "Change of use of 1st, 2nd and third floors to 6 x two bedroom self contained flats, installation of new access from rear of no.28 and the erection of a single storey rear extension to No.28 and change of use of ground floor launderette at no. 28 to A1 use associated with parking spaces and installation of new shopfront to No. 28.",
  "site_name": "26-28",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "02/12/2004",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "22/12/2008",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the flats are occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 7am to 6pm on Mondays to Friday and 9am to 1pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - The use hereby permitted for flats shall not be begun until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.",
    "Condition : 8 - The access doorway to the the ground floor shop at 28 Chiswick High Road shall have a minimum clear width of 900mm, a level surface or ramp between the pavement and the floor and a door handle of not more than 1m above ground level.",
    "Condition : 9 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 10 - That on the satisfactory completion of other aspects of the Section 106 agreements to grant planning permission"
  ],
